{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementations handle their own batching, retry, network failure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and offline queueing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dispatch doesn’t wait for these calls, but the plugin serializes them:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each call starts only after the previous one returns, so they reach the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"service in dispatch order. A call that awaits a network round trip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore holds back every later call. The plugin keeps at most 1,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" calls waiting behind a stalled one and then drops the oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queued "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset"},{"type":"text","text":" are never dropped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Enqueue the work (as vendor SDKs do) and return promptly; do network I\/O"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the service’s own background upload."}]},{"code":["\/\/ Mixpanel implementation lives in SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics:","struct MixpanelAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService { ... }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"cod